{
  "_comment": [
    "Structurally identical fixture of the agency's tracker workbook (AGENCY.md §1).",
    "Shape mirrors the Google Sheets API response: { tabName: string[][] } of raw cell values.",
    "One Instructions tab + one tab per client + the Assigned Media Buyer staffing tab.",
    "Each client tab: header block naming the source of truth, then the DAILY ENTRY table.",
    "Numbers reconcile with SEED.md's weekly figures so the dry-run can prove the mapper.",
    "Birkenstock deliberately STOPS after Jul 9 — the missing-days governance case (flag F3).",
    "NVP values are placeholders pending confirmation of what NVP stands for.",
    "Northbrook uses the agency's real long-date format (\"June 30, 2026\"); others use ISO — the parser is proven against both. NVP carries a % sign, as the real tracker shows it.",
    "Huggers is transcribed from the agency's real tracker screenshot; its Jul 4 and Jul 10 rows contain genuine copy-paste errors, left in deliberately."
  ],
  "Instructions": [
    [
      "RULES — follow these, or things break"
    ],
    [
      "1. One source of truth per client. Named in the client's tab header. Never blend."
    ],
    [
      "2. Type numbers exactly as the source shows them. No rounding, no estimating."
    ],
    [
      "3. Log every day including weekends and zero-spend days. Zeroes, never blanks."
    ],
    [
      "4. Never delete or edit old rows. Flag mistakes to Mitzi."
    ],
    [
      "5. Scan the charts after entry. Flag anomalies to Sultan or the client channel."
    ]
  ],
